#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hearth's desktop portal backend (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.hearth).

xdg-desktop-portal asks a desktop's own backend for what only the desktop
knows; in the arbor session that is this one (share/xdg-desktop-portal/
portals/hearth.portal, routed in /etc/nixos's xdg.portal.config.arbor).
Apps reach it through xdg-desktop-portal, never directly: Flatpaks for
everything, browsers/Electron/Qt/GTK 4 for the colour scheme.

  hearth-portal serve   the backend (D-Bus activated; runs without hearth)
  hearth-portal ui      hearth's relay for the dialogs (services/Portal.qml)

Interfaces:
- Settings: org.freedesktop.appearance color-scheme / accent-color /
  contrast / reduced-motion, from hearth's light/dark and accent
  ($XDG_STATE_HOME/hearth/appearance.json, written by hearth-color-scheme),
  plus every org.gnome.* key set in dconf (fonts, cursor, button layout for
  GTK Flatpaks). SettingChanged when either changes.
- Notification: handed to hearth's notification server
  (org.freedesktop.Notifications), buttons and default action included.
- Lockdown: the GNOME lockdown/privacy keys in dconf (all off by default).
- Account, Access, AppChooser, DynamicLauncher, Print: a hearth sheet
  (popups/PortalDialog.qml). With no hearth running they answer "cancelled".
- Email: opens a mailto: link in almanac (or the default mail app).

The dialog relay: `hearth-portal ui` owns io.github.benwbooth.hearth.PortalUI;
the backend calls its Show(json) / Dismiss(id), and the relay prints those as
JSON lines for the shell. The shell answers on the relay's stdin
({"id": N, "response": 0|1|2, ...}), which the relay passes back with the
backend's Answer(id, json).

Options: --name NAME serves another bus name (tests).
Env: HEARTH_PORTAL_STATE overrides the appearance file (tests).
"""
